SUMMARY:[Hike - Intermediate] Seaton Trail & 3rd Concession
DESCRIPTION:GTA Hiking & Stuff\nValley Farm Dog Park @ Seaton Trail & 3rd 
 Concession -\n\nPLEASE NOTE: This hike starts a the Southern end of the Se
 aton Trail and heads north for about an hour before we turn around. Please
  note the parking location\n\\*\\*\\*\nSeaton Trail is another beautiful h
 iking area up near the Pickering area.\n\nThis time\, we are going to star
 t at the south end of Seaton Trail and head north. This is an intermediate
  hike.\n\nWe will strive for between 7-10 kms. There are some sections wit
 h hills that will get your heart rate up.\n\nBring a water bottle and dres
 s for the weather.\n\nThe hike leaves at 9:35am sharp.\n\nWe will be meeti
 ng at the Seaton Trail Parking Lot off Concession 3 (Rossland Road) ([http
 s://goo.gl/maps/575kQzkHLJP1tx198](https://goo.gl/maps/575kQzkHLJP1tx198))
 . There is a small parking lot. It is a very busy parking lot\, so please 
 arrive early or share ride where possible.\n\nWe will hike at a medium pac
 e (4 - 5 km/h) for the approx 8 kms.\n\nBring 1L of water and good hiking 
 shoes or boots.\n\n**Parking Address:**\nValley Farm Rd. & 3rd Concession 
 · Pickering\, ON\n\nNOTE: Due to construction you can’t take Brock to 3
 rd concession\, you MUST take valley farm road which you can reach from Br
 ock via Dellbrook Ave\, or alternatively via Kingston or Finch Ave.\n\nThe
 re are signs warning of construction\, the trail and parking are open so j
 ust follow the construction signs. At the end of valley farm turn LEFT - T
 he parking lot is not far and on your left.\n\n***Hike starts at 9:35-am S
 HARP.***\n\n**Winter Hiking Season Information:**\n\nPlease note that as w
 e get into winter hiking with snow and slippery trails\, we consider prope
 r Crampons to be mandatory.\nThe event host can ask you not to participate
  if you don't have proper footwear including Crampons. More [Crampon Infor
 mation](https://www.meetup.com/gta-hiking-meetup/events/297067178/).\n\n**
 LEGAL DISCLAIMER AND LIABILITY INFORMATION:**\nBy RSVP'ing and paying the 
 event fee (if applicable)\, you are confirming that you have read\, unders
 tand and accept the following:\n\n1. GTA Hiking Meetup is a private group.
  Attending events is voluntary by you as a member. Participation in any ac
 tivity with us is at your own risk.\n2. By joining this event as a member 
 you agree to indemnify and hold harmless its organizers\, co-organizers\, 
 assistant organizers\, event hosts\, and other members from all claims or 
 liability of every type (including court costs and legal fees) for injury 
 or death to any person or for damage to property\, loss of personal proper
 ty or any other wrongful act arising out of or relating to your participat
 ion as a member. This agreement applies to you and to other persons (as yo
 ur guests) who may accompany you in these endeavours.\n3. You also agree t
 o hold the organizers as well as other group members harmless. By particip
 ating voluntarily in the group\, you expressly waive any and all such clai
 ms against each and every other member in the group\, including without li
 mitation any and all claims against the group organizer\, co-organizers\, 
 assistant organizers\, and event hosts.\n\n**TICK WARNING**\nTicks are sma
 ll bugs that can attach to skin and sometimes spread illnesses like Lyme d
 isease. Learn more at:\n[https://www.canada.ca/en/public-health/services/d
 iseases/lyme-disease/prevention-lyme-disease.html](https://www.canada.ca/e
 n/public-health/services/diseases/lyme-disease/prevention-lyme-disease.htm
 l)
